  "privacyTitle": "Privacy & data",
  "privacyDraftsTitle": "Drafts stay on this device",
  "privacyDraftsBody": "While you write, your draft is saved encrypted on this device only. It is never sent to our servers, and it is deleted when you seal it, discard it, or sign out.",
  "privacySealedTitle": "Sealed messages",
  "privacySealedBody": "When you seal a message we store it with its opening time, time zone and status. Access is enforced by the database itself, not just the app: only your account can see your messages, and nobody, not even you, can read one before it opens.",
  "privacyNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "privacyNotificationsBody": "A notification only says \"A message is ready\". It never contains what you wrote, so nothing private shows on your lock screen. To send it we keep a notification address for this device from Firebase Cloud Messaging, removed when you sign out.",
  "privacyTrackingTitle": "No tracking",
  "privacyTrackingBody": "Laternote has no analytics, ads or crash reporting. Our logs record counts only, never message content.",
  "privacyDeletionTitle": "Deleting your account",
  "privacyDeletionBody": "During this early MVP, account deletion is handled manually: use \"Request account deletion\" on the Account screen to send a request. We delete your account, messages and device addresses by hand, normally within a few business days, and confirm by email.",
  "privacyBackupsTitle": "Backups",
  "privacyBackupsBody": "Encrypted backups age out after about 30 days. If one is ever restored, deletion requests made since then are applied again.",

